public import Theory.GroupTheory.Recognition.ReeTwo.SmallEvenDescentEdgeData
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.ReeTwo.SylowCollectedArithmetic

/-!
# Word witnesses for the recorded small even descent edges

The forward and backward words express each conjugated edge generator in the
target generators and conversely. Rows retain the original 3617-edge order and
both generator families retain their ten-entry padding. Every word has length
at most five. GAP and breadth-first search only supply witnesses; the equations
are checked separately by Lean's kernel in `SmallEvenDescentEdgeCertificates`.

The collected root-word dictionary is proved equal to the existing dictionary,
so the certificate proposition implies `ClosureWords.Valid` for the original
group operations and definitions.

Source: Shinoda (1975), (2.3), pp. 81–82. The input hashes and conventions are
recorded in `SmallEvenDescentEdgeData`. Generation scripts and original inputs
are retained in `Scratch/ree-edge-certificates` of the generating workspace.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace ReeTwo.SylowModel.SmallEvenDescentEdges.Certificates
